<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neuchâtel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neuchâtel is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> on the north shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-neuchatel">Lake Neuchâtel</a>, capital of the canton of the same name. First recorded in 1011, it was ruled by its counts and later the Orléans-Longueville family, and from 1707 by the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> as princes. It joined the Swiss Confederation as a canton in 1815, became a republic in 1848, and Prussia renounced its claims in 1857.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neuchatel.jpg" alt="Neuchâtel" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francoise Kuenzi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vuevilledeneuchatel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
